* Defense to the opponents' two-level and higher openings

Booklet section "DEFENSIVE BIDDING" covers overcalls and doubles of one-level
openings; for the opponents' weak two-bids and preempts it only says that the
same methods apply one level higher. This file writes that out (NOTES.md #P2):
a double is for takeout (short in their suit, 12--16, or any 17+ hand), a
suit overcall is natural with a five-card suit at the two level (10--16) and a
six-card suit at the three level (12--16), 2NT over a weak two is 15--18
balanced with a stopper, 3NT is to play. Over a three-level preempt the double
is for takeout with 13+, a suit overcall needs a six-card suit and 13+, and
3NT is to play with 16--21 and a stopper. A four-level preempt is doubled with
16+ and otherwise passed. Over the strong 2!c and the 2NT opening a natural
overcall needs a good hand and a long suit; everything else passes.

Every table ends in a pass chain (`passes.bml`): once we pass, we keep
passing while the opponents bid on. The advances below end the auction for us
as well (an `after-chain` under each of them): the doubler or overcaller does
not bid again. The booklet gives none of these numbers; they are this file's
interpolation from the one-level methods in `competition.bml`.

** Over a weak two-bid

(2D)-
2N = {prio:3} 15--18 hcp, bal, stopper
3N = {prio:3} 19--21 hcp, stopper
2H = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 5+!h
2S = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 5+!s
3C = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+!c
D = {prio:1} 12--16 hcp and 0--2!d or 17+ hcp
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-
2N = {prio:3} 15--18 hcp, bal, stopper
3N = {prio:3} 19--21 hcp, stopper
2S = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 5+!s
3C = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+!c
3D = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+!d
D = {prio:1} 12--16 hcp and 0--2!h or 17+ hcp
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-
2N = {prio:3} 15--18 hcp, bal, stopper
3N = {prio:3} 19--21 hcp, stopper
3H = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 5+!h
3C = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+!c
3D = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+!d
D = {prio:1} 12--16 hcp and 0--2!s or 17+ hcp
#PASTE pass-chain

In the balancing seat (the opener's partner passed) the same calls can be a
little lighter: the double 10--16 with shortness (or 17+), a suit 8--16.

(2D)-P-(P)-
2N = {prio:3} 14--17 hcp, bal, stopper
2H = {prio:2} 8--16 hcp, 5+!h
2S = {prio:2} 8--16 hcp, 5+!s
3C = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 6+!c
D = {prio:1} 10--16 hcp and 0--2!d or 17+ hcp
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-P-(P)-
2N = {prio:3} 14--17 hcp, bal, stopper
2S = {prio:2} 8--16 hcp, 5+!s
3C = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 6+!c
3D = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 6+!d
D = {prio:1} 10--16 hcp and 0--2!h or 17+ hcp
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-P-(P)-
2N = {prio:3} 14--17 hcp, bal, stopper
3H = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 5+!h
3C = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 6+!c
3D = {prio:2} 10--16 hcp, 6+!d
D = {prio:1} 10--16 hcp and 0--2!s or 17+ hcp
#PASTE pass-chain

*** Advancing the takeout double of a weak two

Advancer bids game in a major with 12+ and four cards, 3NT with 12+ and a
stopper, jumps in a five-card suit with 9--11, and otherwise bids the cheapest
four-card suit (a major first); with none of these (length in their suit)
advancer passes for penalty.

#CUT adv-dbl-2d
4H = {prio:7} 12+ hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
4S = {prio:7} 12+ hcp, 4+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:6} 12+ hcp, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
3H = {prio:5} 9--11 hcp, 5+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
3S = {prio:5} 9--11 hcp, 5+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
2H = {prio:4} 0--11 hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
2S = {prio:4} 0--11 hcp, 4+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
3C = {prio:3} 0--11 hcp, 4+!c
  #PASTE after-chain
2N = {prio:2} 9--11 hcp
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT adv-dbl-2h
4S = {prio:7} 12+ hcp, 4+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:6} 12+ hcp, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
3S = {prio:5} 9--11 hcp, 5+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
2S = {prio:4} 0--11 hcp, 4+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
3C = {prio:3} 0--11 hcp, 4+!c
  #PASTE after-chain
3D = {prio:3} 0--11 hcp, 4+!d
  #PASTE after-chain
2N = {prio:2} 9--11 hcp
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT adv-dbl-2s
4H = {prio:7} 12+ hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:6} 12+ hcp, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
3H = {prio:4} 0--11 hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
3C = {prio:3} 0--11 hcp, 4+!c
  #PASTE after-chain
3D = {prio:3} 0--11 hcp, 4+!d
  #PASTE after-chain
2N = {prio:2} 9--11 hcp
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

(2D)-D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-dbl-2d

(2H)-D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-dbl-2h

(2S)-D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-dbl-2s

(2D)-P-(P)-D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-dbl-2d

(2H)-P-(P)-D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-dbl-2h

(2S)-P-(P)-D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-dbl-2s

When the opener's partner bids over the double, advancer is no longer forced
to bid: he competes in a major with four cards and 6--11, bids game with 12+,
and otherwise passes.

(2D)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

*** Advancing an overcall of a weak two

Advancer raises the overcall with three-card support (a major) or four (a
minor): to the three level with 8--11, to game in a major with 12+; 3NT with
12+ and a stopper in their suit; otherwise pass.

#CUT adv-overcall-major
4\M = {prio:3} 12+ hcp, 3+!\m
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:2} 12+ hcp, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
3\M = {prio:1} 8--11 hcp, 3+!\m
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT adv-overcall-minor
3N = {prio:2} 12+ hcp, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

(2D)-2H-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-major \M=H \m=h

(2D)-2S-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-major \M=S \m=s

(2H)-2S-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-major \M=S \m=s

(2S)-3H-(P)-
4H = {prio:3} 10+ hcp, 3+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:2} 12+ hcp, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain

(2D)-3C-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-minor

(2H)-3C-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-minor

(2H)-3D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-minor

(2S)-3C-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-minor

(2S)-3D-(P)-
#PASTE adv-overcall-minor

Opposite the 2NT overcall (15--18) advancer bids 3NT with 8+, game in a major
with a six-card suit and 8+, and otherwise passes.

#CUT adv-2n-overcall
4H = {prio:2} 8+ hcp, 6+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
4S = {prio:2} 8+ hcp, 6+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:1} 8+ hcp
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

(2D)-2N-(P)-
#PASTE adv-2n-overcall

(2H)-2N-(P)-
#PASTE adv-2n-overcall

(2S)-2N-(P)-
#PASTE adv-2n-overcall

Advancer passes 3NT, and passes after any bid by the opener's partner.

(2D)-3N-
#PASTE after-chain

(2H)-3N-
#PASTE after-chain

(2S)-3N-
#PASTE after-chain

(2D)-2H-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2D)-2S-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-2S-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-3H-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2D)-3C-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-3C-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-3D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-3C-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-3D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2D)-2N-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2H)-2N-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

(2S)-2N-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

